#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087504 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63a7522-8d05-5d3a-aafb-3450292f910f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Components of a Linear Map"}] :question/id #uuid "ae56bd17-f7f2-5c66-ac2a-663f05c6a838" :question/math-academy-id "e-5518" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\to \\mathbb{R}^3$ shown above. What is the value of $a-b$?" :question/worked-solution "Given the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}-8x - 5y \\\\ -3x - 6y \\\\ -4x + 5y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-5y - 8x \\\\ -3x - 6y \\\\ 5y - 4x\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\na-b=(-5)-(-4)=-1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087505 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb96cd29-b9f6-5b68-b43e-4a55ef8ffab2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map"}] :question/id #uuid "0ae354ba-19f3-570c-bbfc-56dd5dbbafa8" :question/math-academy-id "e-5519" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2$, find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})$.\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\,\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})=T\\cdot \\mathbf{v}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nT(v) &= T \\cdot v \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087519 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e35b58a-530f-5b9b-8df2-eb737f8af581" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "9c24c0bb-f779-5518-8c44-70b3e51065a2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5901" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "We require a $2\\times 3$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nNotice that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088102 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb96cd29-b9f6-5b68-b43e-4a55ef8ffab2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b69459d5-3498-5323-9134-c7fc3e0185e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085544} {:answer/id #uuid "de6b3660-9bcc-55ab-8c64-7f1534ba5986" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085545} {:answer/id #uuid "15100286-887b-5cb4-aaf3-3ea9a1a0f87a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085546} {:answer/id #uuid "38486145-1630-5f9c-bd25-91e4ec0b1979" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085547} {:answer/id #uuid "5bc61647-6083-5c9c-8f5b-4f80c59826ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type